One Small Robustness Fix

Your current code assumes root != null.

This:

if(isLeaf(root)==false)

would throw a NullPointerException if root == null.

A safer version is:

public ArrayList<Integer> boundaryTraversal(Node root) {

    ArrayList<Integer> al = new ArrayList<>();

    if (root == null) {
        return al;
    }

    if (!isLeaf(root)) {
        al.add(root.data);
    }

    addLeftBoundry(root, al);
    addLeaves(root, al);
    addRightBoundry(root, al);

    return al;
}

