Approach 4 — Morris Traversal / O(1) Auxiliary Space

This is an advanced version.

The standard recursive solution is already optimal in time:

O(n)

but it uses:

O(h)

call-stack space.

A Morris-based solution can perform the leaf traversal without an auxiliary DFS stack, giving:

O(n) time
O(1) auxiliary space

apart from the output list.

This is useful to know for interviews that explicitly ask for constant auxiliary space, but it is considerably harder to remember and explain.

Code
import java.util.*;

class Solution {

    boolean isLeaf(Node root) {
        return root.left == null && root.right == null;
    }

    public ArrayList<Integer> boundaryTraversal(Node root) {

        ArrayList<Integer> ans = new ArrayList<>();

        if (root == null) {
            return ans;
        }

        // Special case: root itself is the only boundary/leaf
        if (isLeaf(root)) {
            ans.add(root.data);
            return ans;
        }

        // Root
        ans.add(root.data);

        // -----------------------------
        // 1. Left boundary
        // -----------------------------
        Node curr = root.left;

        while (curr != null) {

            if (!isLeaf(curr)) {
                ans.add(curr.data);
            }

            if (curr.left != null) {
                curr = curr.left;
            } else {
                curr = curr.right;
            }
        }

        // -----------------------------
        // 2. Leaves using Morris
        // -----------------------------
        curr = root;

        while (curr != null) {

            if (curr.left == null) {

                // If no left and no right, curr is a leaf
                if (curr.right == null) {
                    ans.add(curr.data);
                }

                curr = curr.right;

            } else {

                Node predecessor = curr.left;

                while (predecessor.right != null
                        && predecessor.right != curr) {
                    predecessor = predecessor.right;
                }

                if (predecessor.right == null) {

                    // Create temporary thread
                    predecessor.right = curr;
                    curr = curr.left;

                } else {

                    // Remove temporary thread
                    predecessor.right = null;

                    // If predecessor has no left child,
                    // it was a leaf.
                    if (predecessor.left == null) {
                        ans.add(predecessor.data);
                    }

                    curr = curr.right;
                }
            }
        }

        // -----------------------------
        // 3. Right boundary
        // -----------------------------
        int rightStart = ans.size();

        curr = root.right;

        while (curr != null) {

            if (!isLeaf(curr)) {
                ans.add(curr.data);
            }

            if (curr.right != null) {
                curr = curr.right;
            } else {
                curr = curr.left;
            }
        }

        // Reverse right boundary in-place
        int left = rightStart;
        int right = ans.size() - 1;

        while (left < right) {

            int temp = ans.get(left);
            ans.set(left, ans.get(right));
            ans.set(right, temp);

            left++;
            right--;
        }

        return ans;
    }
}

Complexity
Time  = O(n)
Space = O(1) auxiliary

The output list itself requires O(n) space, of course.

